WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:03.310
(gentle piano music)

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:04.990
- There's a weird phenomenon I've noticed

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.090
all throughout my life

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.440
where the more I subject
myself to discomfort,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.840
the happier I am.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.240
I think this phenomenon became
increasingly apparent to me

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.090
in first year of university,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:19.040
where I wanted to make the
best impression possible.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.050
You know, typical freshman behavior.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.260
It's a new school, new network of people,

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.220
new city, so I really felt a need

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.800
to reinvent who I was as a human being,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.630
especially on a kind
of social skills basis.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.250
So in order to do that,
I was forcing myself

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.580
outside of my comfort zone so frequently,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.480
it's as if it was some sort of game.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.350
It's like I was able to
peel back a layer of reality

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.340
and see some sort of
one-to-one relationship

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.240
between subjecting myself to discomfort

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.550
and upgrading who I was as a human being.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.390
Now that I'm in my old age,
I don't necessarily think

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.160
that is a one-to-one
relationship, more on that later,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.940
but I was definitely onto something,

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.680
because I felt incredible.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.750
I was energetic, optimistic,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.210
I remember waking up in
the morning not being tired

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.750
because I was ready to
tackle the day with energy,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.410
and although this euphoria
didn't last forever,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.130
I never forgot how I felt.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:12.730
And I remember the importance
of viewing the comfort zone

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.860
and the effect it has on
your overall wellbeing

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.430
and the way you live your life.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.580
So in this video, we're gonna talk

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.290
about a few things that I've learned

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.170
about the comfort zone, and how I think

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.190
if you can gain a better understanding

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.910
of how the comfort zone works,

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.150
you can start living life on your terms

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.500
instead of its terms.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.010
Because it has a lot more control

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.400
over the way you live your
life than you might think.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.670
So here are some things

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.400
that I've discovered
about the comfort zone,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.420
and hopefully, you can apply
them to your life, as well.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.670
So everything you're
physically capable of doing

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.460
in this world falls into
one of two categories:

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.660
inside the comfort zone or
outside the comfort zone.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.618
The things that are
inside the comfort zone

00:01:49.618 --> 00:01:52.700
are easy for you to do, comfortable,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.920
they take little or no effort to do,

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.830
and there's pretty much
no mental resistance

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:00.020
in the way of doing that
thing, like driving.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.350
For a lot of people, driving

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.300
is completely in the comfort zone.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.100
You know, you drive to work,
you drive to your house,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.758
you drive to the store to
pretend to buy vitamins

00:02:08.758 --> 00:02:10.860
so you can get footage for this video.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.080
Since driving is so easy,
at one point or another,

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.030
your brain went and
subconsciously placed it

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.550
inside the comfort zone.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.370
So you don't really think about doing it

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.650
before you do it, it's
just something you do.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.720
Okay, how about going for a run?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.810
A lot harder, isn't it?

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.438
It's more physically strenuous,

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:31.210
requires more preparation,
it makes you lose your breath

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.580
or sweat, and if you
haven't ran for a while,

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.710
you'll probably be
really sore the next day.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.700
And because you know running
is physically strenuous,

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.371
and hard to do, your brain
at one point or another

00:02:41.371 --> 00:02:44.120
went and placed it
outside the comfort zone.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.730
The further outside the
comfort zone something is,

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.740
the more mental resistance there is

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.980
in the way of doing that thing.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.100
But here's where things
get kind of interesting.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.840
Running is good for you.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.660
After a week of running every day,

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.060
you can find that your
mental energy increases,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.340
your outlook on life is better

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.950
and more optimistic, and
after a week of driving,

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.350
you kind of feel nothing.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.580
It's just driving.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.240
So there really isn't a
clear cut relationship

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.420
between things that are
inside the comfort zone,

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.770
outside the comfort zone,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.660
and the value that these
things have on your life.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.050
In fact, the comfort zone is terrible

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.650
at telling you what's good for you

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.810
and what's bad for you.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.092
What activities you should
adopt into your life

00:03:22.092 --> 00:03:24.190
and what activities you should avoid.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.020
So let's take walking, for example.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.900
Walking is probably
inside your comfort zone,

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.500
and running is outside of it.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.520
But it doesn't mean that
walking is bad for you,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.770
in the same way stabbing
yourself in the leg

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.218
with a pencil is probably
outside of your comfort zone

00:03:37.218 --> 00:03:38.870
but it doesn't mean it's good for you.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.520
So there really isn't a
clear cut relationship

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.680
between things that are
inside the comfort zone,

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.060
outside the comfort zone,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.870
and the value that these
things have on your life.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.400
All the comfort zone is concerned with

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.190
is keeping you inside of it.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.590
And the way it does that is

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:56.150
not only does it make sure
that things outside of it

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.400
are really uncomfortable and hard to do,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.310
it's also always shrinking

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.790
if you don't do anything about it.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.330
Unless you venture at least a little bit

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.370
beyond the borders of the comfort zone,

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.710
it will get smaller and harder to escape.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.230
And this is something that most people

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.560
have experienced in their lives,

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.220
whether they're aware of it or not.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.700
In my own life, this happens all the time.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.093
Like when Halo Five came
out a few years ago,

00:04:18.093 --> 00:04:20.830
I spent so much time just playing it

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.500
for hours and hours every day,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.380
eating Doritos Sweet Chili Heat

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.550
and drinking Mountain
Dew like a real gamer,

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.220
and after days of doing this,

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.230
binging a video game and not doing

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.240
anything outside of my comfort zone,

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.510
things that were
previously just on the edge

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.410
of my comfort zone, like going to the gym,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.010
the comfort zone shrank to a point

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.650
where going to the gym was
now extremely difficult

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:44.120
and very hard to bring myself to do.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.134
You may have also experienced
this type of thing

00:04:46.134 --> 00:04:48.610
where maybe you're on vacation,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.900
and it's sort of one of those sit around

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.150
and don't really do much vacations,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.530
you're kind of on your phone a lot,

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.580
on the couch, maybe the
weather's really nice,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.270
and you start to become soft, you know?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.133
You don't really want to
do many interesting things

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.480
or very hard things or anything

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.770
that would take much effort.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.630
You kind of just become a blob

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.670
and you feel pathetic.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.000
Okay, so what have we learned?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.090
We've learned that in order
to keep the comfort zone

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.643
from shrinking, we have to do things

00:05:14.643 --> 00:05:16.680
that are outside of the comfort zone

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.260
to keep the comfort zone large.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.890
But we also learned that
the comfort zone in general

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.130
is a pretty terrible guide for telling us

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.300
what to do with our life,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.210
what activities are useful to us

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.470
and what activities
don't really do anything.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.170
So basically, we need a
solution to this problem.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.960
We need a more reliable
guide for making decisions.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.710
And I think you can't go wrong

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.400
with making values based decisions.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.500
Your values.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.900
Figure out what kind of
person you want to be,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.320
what kind of traits you want to adopt,

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.440
what kind of skills you want to learn,

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.030
and make your decisions based off of that.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.420
And using the knowledge
of the comfort zone,

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.150
be aware that any potential discomfort

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.040
in the way of doing the
thing that you want to do

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.960
isn't a real obstacle,
it's all just in your head.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.040
If you live life this
way, the comfort zone

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.680
can also work in your favor

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.960
because as you start
living this new lifestyle

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.620
that may have at first
been unnatural to you,

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.280
the longer you live that way,

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.200
the comfort zone is expanding to meet you.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.820
So living the way you want to live

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.870
will become increasingly natural

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.870
and, dare I say, comfortable.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:21.900
So to bring this whole thing

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.650
back to my freshman year,
it's becoming clear to me that

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.440
the reason I felt so good

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.080
wasn't necessarily because I was

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.970
just uncomfortable all the time.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.210
The reason I felt so good

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:33.350
was because I was living the life

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:34.520
that I wanted to live

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.900
and I disregarded discomfort altogether.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.040
And when you no longer let discomfort

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.950
have a say in how you make
any of your decisions,

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:44.359
the potential for what
you can do with your life

00:06:44.359 --> 00:06:46.593
expands dramatically.

